---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { levels, lessonCount } from '../data/curriculum.js';
import { finderPromise } from '../data/quiz.js';
import { glossary } from '../data/glossary.js';

// RESTRUCTURED 2026-07-28 (twice). First: this page stopped being an eight-step
// ACTION path and became the syllabus — its action steps moved to the checklist,
// its teaching prose stayed. Then: the syllabus became LEVELS, reading from
// curriculum.js, so the mega-menu, this page, the prev/next footer, and the
// /learn index can never disagree about what the course contains.

const termCount = glossary.length;
---
<Base
  title="Start here — the whole guide, in order · BitcoinKeys.guide"
  description={`Brand new to holding your own Bitcoin? This is the whole guide laid out in teaching order — ${lessonCount} lessons across ${levels.length} levels, from what a key actually is, through how people lose Bitcoin, to the ladder of real setups.`}
  verified="2026-08-04"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Start here · the whole course</p>
    <h1>The whole guide, <span class="accent">in the order it makes sense</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">If you just bought Bitcoin and want to hold it yourself, you’re in the right place. This is the map: {lessonCount} short lessons across {levels.length} levels, each building on the one before. No jargon dumped on you, and nothing you have to decide yet.</p>

    {/* Principle 0 on the surface the Foundation claims enforces it. Stated in the
        SYLLABUS's own terms — why a course exists at all — not as a repeat of the
        home page's full statement. Detail lives in one place; this is the door. */}
    <p>Reading is the point, and it is worth saying why before you start. <strong>There is nothing you can buy that makes you safe.</strong> A hardware wallet is a tool in the hands of someone who understands it, and almost every loss this course can teach you about happened to somebody who owned the right equipment and did not know one thing about how it worked. That is why this is a course rather than a shopping list — and why the setup you can explain to someone else is the one that is still standing years from now.</p>

    <div class="callout">
      {/* NOT "the one idea underneath all of it" (until 2026-07-30). That slot
          belongs to the umbrella in rules.js — "Verify. Don't trust." — and the
          home page was claiming it for rule 03 at the same time. This callout is
          the invitation into the course, not a competing foundation: it states
          the trade-off, rule 03 states the directive that follows from it. */}
      <span class="label">The trade-off in every choice</span>
      <p>Every custody choice trades off <strong>losing access yourself</strong> against <strong>someone else getting access</strong>. Almost every safeguard against one makes the other worse. You don’t need zero risk — you need risks you can <em>name</em>. That’s what this course is for.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="sub" style="margin-top:1.1rem">Read it in order if you can — each level assumes the one above it. It’s a couple of hours end to end — an evening, not a weekend — and you’ll understand your own setup better than most people who already have one. Every lesson points to the next, so you never have to find your place again.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="syl">
      {levels.map((lv) => (
        <div class:list={['syl-lv', { opt: lv.optional }]} id={lv.id}>
          <span class="syl-badge">{lv.id}</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="syl-h">{lv.title}{lv.optional && <span class="syl-opt">· optional</span>}</h2>
            <p class="syl-why">{lv.why}</p>
            <ol class="syl-list">
              {lv.lessons.map((l) => (
                <li><a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>{l.note && <em>{l.note}</em>}</li>
              ))}
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Two things to keep open beside you</h2>
    <p class="sub prose" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem;">Not lessons — lookups. Reach for them any time a word stops you.</p>
    <div class="grid cols-2">
      <a href="/glossary" class="card">
        <h3>Glossary →</h3>
        <p class="sub">Every term on this site in plain English — {termCount} of them. If a word here isn’t explained where you meet it, it’s explained there.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/resources" class="card">
        <h3>Further reading →</h3>
        <p class="sub">The genuinely good outside material — books, tools, and references worth your time, with none of the noise.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="sub flat-note">Prefer one flat list instead of levels? <a href="/learn">Every lesson on one page →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="callout safe">
      <span class="label">Where this gets you</span>
      <p>By the end of level 102 you’ll be able to say, in one sentence, which setup fits you and why — and just as importantly, which ones you <em>don’t</em> need. That’s the whole game. The simplest setup you fully understand and have tested beats an impressive one you don’t.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="handoff">
      <p class="ho-k mono">When you’re ready to build it</p>
      <p>The reading is the hard part; the doing is a checklist. When this all makes sense — or if you’d rather see where you’d land first — finding your setup is {finderPromise} — it names the one that fits you, then turns it into a step-by-step checklist. <strong>It never asks how much Bitcoin you hold</strong>, and it runs entirely in your browser.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        {/* Course entry carries the primary style, the finder rides ghost —
            swapped 2026-08-04. This is the syllabus page of an education-first
            site, and its loudest element was the door PAST the course.
            /learn/rules, not /learn/bitcoin-keys — the syllabus above lists the
            rules as lesson 1 and tags them "read first"; this button used to
            start the reader at lesson 2. */}
        <a href="/learn/rules" class="btn btn-primary">Start level 101 <span class="arw">→</span></a>
        <a href="/find-your-setup" class="btn btn-ghost">Find your setup</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .syl { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem; }
  .syl-lv { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface);
    padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3.6rem 1fr; gap: 1.3rem;
    scroll-margin-top: 4.5rem; }
  /* A dashed edge says "skippable" before you read a word. Applies to any level
     flagged `optional`; none is, since 201 was removed 2026-08-01. */
  .syl-lv.opt { border-style: dashed; }
  .syl-badge { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--accent-ink);
    background: var(--accent); border-radius: 0.55rem; height: 2.3rem; display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .syl-lv.opt .syl-badge { background: var(--safe); }
  .syl-h { margin: 0 0 0.15rem; font-size: 1.14rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .syl-opt { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--safe);
    margin-left: 0.5rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .syl-why { margin: 0 0 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.93rem; max-width: 62ch; }
  .syl-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.35rem 1.2rem; counter-reset: none; }
  .syl-list li { font-size: 0.92rem; display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: baseline; }
  .syl-list li::before { content: "›"; color: var(--accent); flex: 0 0 auto; }
  .syl-lv.opt .syl-list li::before { color: var(--safe); }
  .syl-list a { text-decoration: none; color: var(--text); }
  .syl-list a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .syl-list em { color: var(--faint); font-style: normal; font-size: 0.8rem; }

  .flat-note { margin-top: 1.1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .handoff { border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--accent-soft);
    padding: 1.5rem 1.7rem; margin-top: 1.8rem; }
  .handoff .ho-k { display: block; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.74rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .handoff p { margin: 0; }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 1.3rem; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .syl-lv { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.7rem; }
    .syl-badge { width: 3.2rem; }
  }
</style>
